  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8ef4a382a350f98438c21cfd3c789fdf, type: 3}
  m_Name: Shapes1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  lessonTitle: Shapes 1
  lessonId: shapes1
  slides:
  - slideName: Slide 1
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: In this lesson, we will learn about some common survival shapes. Survival
      shapes are usually small and can create two eyes easily.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 2
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: This shape is called a "straight three". Its survival depends on who
      goes first if black goes first at the highlighted location, black lives with
      two eyes.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 3
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: However, if white goes first, it can "pop" the two eyes. Even if black
      captures the center white stone, it cannot get two eyes back.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 4
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: This shape is called a "bent three". Its survival also depends on who
      goes first.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 5
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: We're moving on to the fours now. This is called a "nail four". Its
      survival, again, depends on who goes first.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 6
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: This is called a "straight four". This time, however, it can survive
      even if white goes first. If white plays at 1, black can make two eyes by playing
      at 2. If white plays at 2, black can do so at 1.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 7
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: From left to right, these are called a "bent four" and a "lightning
      four". They can live even if white goes first for the same reason as the straight
      four. Shapes that survive even if the opponent attacks first are called "living
      shapes".
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 8
    slideType: 1
    bodyText: Now it's your turn. Make your shape live!
    boardSource: 0
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 4900000, guid: 1901ff7c7c31f7447ab06cc0dcb93da8, type: 3}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 9
    slideType: 1
    bodyText: Make your shape live!
    boardSource: 0
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 4900000, guid: f484414d1ddec924aacbfda69a2fa887, type: 3}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
